<title>IVORY COAST: IVORY COAST GOVERNMENT LIST (970811).</title>
<headline>IVORY COAST GOVERNMENT LIST (970811).</headline>
<text>
<p>IVORY COAST GOVERNMENT LIST (970811)</p>
<p>President...................................Henri KONAN BEDIE</p>
<p>(Elected for a five-year term 22 Oct 95)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>DEMOCRATIC PARTY OF IVORY COAST (PDCI)-DOMINATED GOVERNMENT:</p>
<p>(Formed 26 January 1996, Reshuffled 10 Aug 96)</p>
<p>(All members of the PDCI except Culture minister ZADI</p>
<p>who is from the Union of Social Democrats (USD))</p>
<p>Prime Minister (appointed 11 dec 93,</p>
<p>reappointed 24 jan 96)...............Daniel Kablan DUNCAN</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Planning and Industrial Development)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS OF STATE: in charge of Relations with National</p>
<p>Institutions.....................Timothee AHOUA Nguetta</p>
<p>National Solidarity......................Laurent DONA FOLOGO</p>
<p>(Also Secretary General of the PDCI-elected 15 Apr 91)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS: Agriculture &amp; Livestock................Lambert KOUASSI KONAN</p>
<p>Commerce................................Nicolas Akon KOUASSI</p>
<p>Commodities.........................Guy-Alain Emmanuel GAUZE</p>
<p>Communication (Information)............Daniele BONI CLAVERIE</p>
<p>Culture...........................Bernard ZADI Zaourou (USD)</p>
<p>Defence......................................Bandama N'GATTA</p>
<p>Development of Crafts..................Lancine Gon COULIBALY</p>
<p>Economic Infrastructure...........................Ezan AKELE</p>
<p>Economy &amp; Finance.............................Ngoran NIAMIEN</p>
<p>Education.......................................Pierre KIPRE</p>
<p>Employment &amp; Civil Service.......................Atchi ATSIN</p>
<p>Family &amp; Promotion of Women.........Albertine GNANAZAN Hepie</p>
<p>Foreign Affairs...................................Amara ESSY</p>
<p>Higher Education, Research &amp; Technological</p>
<p>Innovation..................................Saliou TOURE</p>
<p>Housing and Environment.................Albert Kakou TIAPANI</p>
<p>Interior...............................Emile Constant BOMBET</p>
<p>Justice.........................................Brou KOUAKOU</p>
<p>Mines &amp; Energy.................................Lamine FADIKA</p>
<p>Presidential Affairs..........................Faustin KOUAME</p>
<p>Public Health.........................Maurice Kakou GUIKAHUE</p>
<p>Security.................................Marcel Dibonan KONE</p>
<p>Sports.....................................Siguide SOUMAHORO</p>
<p>Technical instruction &amp; professional training..Komenan ZAKPA Youth &amp; Civic Culture...........................Vlami Bi DOU</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Deputy minister in the prime minister's office, responsible</p>
<p>for Planning and Industrial Development.....Ahoua N'DOLI Deputy minister at the agriculture ministry, responsible for</p>
<p>promotion of young famers................Amadou OUATTARA</p>
<p>Deputy minister at the economic infrastructure ministry,</p>
<p>responsible for energy and transport......Safiatou N'DAW</p>
<p>High Commission for Tourism.....................Kindo BOUADY</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Speaker of Parliament ...............Emile Brou Amoakon ATTA</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Central Bank Governor....................Charles Konan BANNY</p>
<p>(Central Bank of West African States)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
